These scripts can be used along with the phyluce harvest from genomes tutorial (Faircloth et al. 2017; https://phyluce.readthedocs.io/en/latest/tutorials/tutorial-3.html)

How to use:

1.	Convert fasta genomes to .2bit
gunzip x.fasta.gz
faToTwoBit -ignoreDups x.fasta x.2bit
twoBitInfo x.2bit sizes.tab
2.	Create folder named after genome with .tab and .2bit files
3.	01_uce_search.slurm 
4.	Update genomes.conf with sample names and path of each file
5.	Run 02_uce_extraction.slurm with x amount of flanking regions}
6.	Explode by loci
phyluce_assembly_explode_get_fastas_file \
--input all-taxa-incomplete.fasta \
    --output exploded-fastas \

You will end up with UCE references that you can use for SNP calling in step 03_intraspecific_diversity
